# OpenAPI spec snippets → generated Kora 2.x server code

Copy-paste fragments for a `java-server` / `kotlin-server` contract, each paired with what the
`kora` generator actually emits. Placeholders are `${...}`.
Full working contract: `openapi-spec.yaml.template`.

## 1. A tagged operation

```yaml
tags:
  - name: ${tag}                       # -> ${Tag}ApiDelegate / ${Tag}ApiResponses / ${Tag}ApiController

paths:
  /${resource}/{id}:
    get:
      tags: ["${tag}"]
      operationId: get${Resource}ById  # -> method name, and the response type prefix
      parameters:
        - name: id
          in: path
          required: true
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int64
      responses:
        '200':
          description: Found
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/${Resource}'
        '404':
          description: Not found
```

```java
// generated
${Tag}ApiResponses.Get${Resource}ByIdApiResponse get${Resource}ById(@Path("id") long id) throws Exception;

sealed interface Get${Resource}ByIdApiResponse {
  record Get${Resource}ById200ApiResponse(${Resource} content) implements … { }
  record Get${Resource}ById404ApiResponse() implements … { }
}
```

## 2. Exactly one response — no sealed hierarchy

```yaml
      responses:
        '200':
          description: Ok
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: string
```

```java
// generated: a record directly, NOT a nested per-status type
record WhoAmIApiResponse(String content) { }
```

## 3. A `default` response

```yaml
      responses:
        '204':
          description: Deleted
        default:
          description: Unexpected error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'
```

```java
// `int statusCode` is the FIRST component of a default response record
new DeletePetApiResponse.DeletePetDefaultApiResponse(409, new ErrorResponse("conflict"));
```

Status-code **ranges** (`4XX`, `5XX`) work the same way: the record takes the real status first.

```java
new ListPetsApiResponse.ListPets4XXApiResponse(422, new ErrorResponse("invalid filter"));
```

## 4. Response headers

```yaml
      responses:
        '200':
          description: Page of results
          headers:
            x-total-count:
              required: true
              schema: { type: string }
            x-next-page:
              schema: { type: string }         # not required -> may be passed null
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: array
                items:
                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/${Resource}'
```

```java
// headers become trailing components of the response record, written by the generated mapper
record List200ApiResponse(List<${Resource}> content, String xTotalCount, String xNextPage) { }
```

An undeclared header cannot be set from the delegate — declare it in the contract.

## 5. Required, optional, nullable

```yaml
components:
  schemas:
    ${Resource}:
      type: object
      required:
        - id
        - name
        - nickname
      properties:
        id:        { type: integer, format: int64 }   # required        -> long / Long
        name:      { type: string }                   # required        -> String
        tag:       { type: string }                   # optional        -> @Nullable String / String?
        weight:    { type: number, nullable: true }   # optional+null   -> JsonNullable<BigDecimal>
        nickname:  { type: string, nullable: true }   # required+null   -> nullable + @JsonInclude(ALWAYS)
```

`JsonNullable` (`io.koraframework.json.common.JsonNullable`) distinguishes absent from
explicit-null — the correct shape for `PATCH` bodies. There is no `enableJsonNullable` option in
2.0; the rule above is automatic.

## 6. Enums with wire values that differ from the constants

```yaml
        status:
          type: string
          enum: [available, pending, sold]
```

```java
// generated: constants AVAILABLE / PENDING / SOLD, wire values "available" / "pending" / "sold"
public static ${Resource}.StatusEnum fromValue(String value) { … throw new IllegalArgumentException(…); }
```

Parse with `fromValue`, never `Enum.valueOf`; catch `IllegalArgumentException` and return the
contract's `400`.

## 7. Validation constraints

```yaml
        name:
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 64          # -> @Size(min = 1, max = 64)
        age:
          type: integer
          minimum: 0
          maximum: 150           # min AND max -> @Range(from = 0.0, to = 150.0, boundary = INCLUSIVE_INCLUSIVE)
        quantity:
          type: integer
          minimum: 1             # min only, integral -> @Min(1L)
        code:
          type: string
          pattern: '^[A-Z]{3}$'  # -> @Pattern("^[A-Z]{3}$")
```

Only **one** constraint annotation is generated per property, from the chain
`minimum/maximum` → `minLength/maxLength` → `minItems/maxItems` → `pattern` → `$ref`. A string
with both `maxLength` and `pattern` gets `@Size` only; enforce the rest in the delegate.
Requires `configOptions.enableServerValidation: "true"` plus `validation-module` +
`ValidationModule`.

## 8. Security schemes

```yaml
security:
  - BearerAuth: []                    # global default for every operation

components:
  securitySchemes:
    BearerAuth:                       # -> ApiSecurity.BearerAuth
      type: http
      scheme: bearer
    ApiKeyAuth:                       # -> ApiSecurity.ApiKeyAuth
      type: apiKey
      in: header
      name: X-API-KEY
    OAuth:                            # -> ApiSecurity.OAuth
      type: oauth2
      flows:
        clientCredentials:
          tokenUrl: https://auth.example.com/token
          scopes:
            pets:read: Read pets
```

```java
@Tag(ApiSecurity.BearerAuth.class)
default HttpServerPrincipalExtractor<String, Principal> bearerExtractor() { … }
```

Per-operation overrides:

```yaml
      security:
        - BearerAuth: []
        - ApiKeyAuth: []              # OR — either credential authenticates
```

```yaml
      security:
        - cookieAuth1: []
          cookieAuth2: []             # AND — one extractor for the pair, taking a generated
                                      #       ApiSecurity.CookieAuth1WithCookieAuth2AuthData
```

```yaml
      security:
        - BearerAuth: []
        - {}                          # anonymous fallback: the interceptor lets the request through
```

```yaml
      security: []                    # opt this operation out of the global requirement entirely
```

## 9. Discriminated polymorphism

```yaml
    ${Base}:
      type: object
      required: [kind]
      properties:
        kind: { type: string }
      discriminator:
        propertyName: kind
        mapping:
          variant_a: '#/components/schemas/${VariantA}'
          variant_b: '#/components/schemas/${VariantB}'

    ${VariantA}:
      allOf:
        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/${Base}'
        - type: object
          required: [fieldA]
          properties:
            fieldA: { type: string }
```

```java
@Json
@JsonDiscriminatorField("kind")
public sealed interface ${Base} permits ${VariantA}, ${VariantB} { }

@JsonDiscriminatorValue({"variant_a"})
public record ${VariantA}(String kind, String fieldA) implements ${Base} { }
```

Handle it with an exhaustive `switch` / `when`. The discriminator property must exist on the base
schema and be `required`.

## 10. Form and multipart bodies

```yaml
      requestBody:
        content:
          multipart/form-data:
            schema:
              type: object
              required: [name]
              properties:
                name:  { type: string }
                photo: { type: string, format: binary }
```

```java
// form fields are grouped into a record nested in the CONTROLLER, passed via a generated mapper
${Tag}ApiResponses.UploadApiResponse upload(
    @Mapping(${Tag}ApiServerRequestMappers.UploadFormParamRequestMapper.class)
    ${Tag}ApiController.UploadFormParam form) throws Exception;
```

Array form fields are collected part by part (an absent optional array is `null`); boolean form
values accept only `true` / `false`, anything else answers `400`.

## 11. Raw and binary bodies

```yaml
      requestBody:
        content:
          application/octet-stream:
            schema:
              type: string
              format: binary
```

```java
// non-JSON body -> a leading HttpHeaders parameter is added so you can read the real Content-Type
${Tag}ApiResponses.UploadApiResponse upload(HttpHeaders _headers, byte[] body) throws Exception;
```

A bare `type: object` with no schema follows `configOptions.rawBodyMode`
(`BYTES` → `byte[]`, `BODY` → `HttpBodyInput`, `OBJECT` → `Object`).

## 12. Type / format cheat sheet

```yaml
        asString:   { type: string }                            # String
        asUuid:     { type: string, format: uuid }              # java.util.UUID
        asUri:      { type: string, format: uri }               # java.net.URI
        asDate:     { type: string, format: date }              # java.time.LocalDate
        asDateTime: { type: string, format: date-time }         # java.time.OffsetDateTime, or the typeMappings target
        asBinary:   { type: string, format: binary }            # byte[] / ByteArray
        asInt:      { type: integer, format: int32 }            # int / Int
        asLong:     { type: integer, format: int64 }            # long / Long
        asDecimal:  { type: number }                            # java.math.BigDecimal
        asDouble:   { type: number, format: double }            # double / Double
        asBool:     { type: boolean }                           # boolean / Boolean
        asList:     { type: array, items: { type: string } }    # List<String>
        asMap:                                                  # Map<String, String>
          type: object
          additionalProperties: { type: string }
        asFreeForm:                                             # Map<String, Object> / Map<String, Any>
          type: object
          additionalProperties: true
        asEnumList:                                             # List<Model.AsEnumListEnum>
          type: array
          items: { type: string, enum: [a, b] }
```

`date-time` switches to `Instant` / `ZonedDateTime` / `LocalDateTime` through the task's
`typeMappings = ["DateTime": "java.time.Instant"]`.
